     "body": "<p><span class=\"error\">&#91;Followup from Sourceforge Tracker&#93;</span><br/>\nFollowup Submitter: fcswa<br/>\nLogged In: YES <br/>\nuser_id=1855086<br/>\nOriginator: NO</p>\n\n<p>This is just to track SRB module issues prior to the \"official\" target release<br/>\nwith Fedora 2.2.</p>\n\n<ul class=\"alternate\" type=\"square\">\n\t<li>I have been unable to get the SRB module to work when Fedora (2.1.1) is<br/>\nlocated behind a NAT'ed router. If you are behind a firewall, you must open a<br/>\nminimum range of 16 ports and specify that port range in fedora.fcfg.</li>\n\t<li>The rebuilder utility does not yet work with an SRB lowlevel store.</li>\n\t<li>There appear to be two regression bugs: one related to Multipart POSTs when<br/>\nssl is not configured and a one related to the<br/>\nDisseminationService/ExternalContentManager returning 500/403 errors.</li>\n</ul>\n",
